## A streamlined .gitignore for modern .NET projects
## including temporary files, build results, and
## files generated by popular .NET tools. If you are
## developing with Visual Studio, the VS .gitignore
## https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/VisualStudio.gitignore
## has more thorough IDE-specific entries.
##
## Get latest from https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Dotnet.gitignore

# Build results
[Dd]ebug/
[Dd]ebugPublic/
[Rr]elease/
[Rr]eleases/
x64/
x86/
[Ww][Ii][Nn]32/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]64/
bld/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/

# .NET Core
project.lock.json
project.fragment.lock.json
artifacts/

# ASP.NET Scaffolding
ScaffoldingReadMe.txt

# NuGet Packages
*.nupkg
# NuGet Symbol Packages
*.snupkg

# dotenv environment variables file
.env

# Others
~$*
*~
CodeCoverage/

# MSBuild Binary and Structured Log
*.binlog

# MSTest test Results
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
[Bb]uild[Ll]og.*

# NUnit
*.VisualState.xml
TestResult.xml
nunit-*.xml

## A streamlined .gitignore for projects using IJFW (It Just F*cking Works)
## Ferrox Labs' shared development infrastructure for AI-driven teams.
## It separates runtime state (.ijfw/, local-only) from committed
## team conventions, and keeps intermediate artifacts out of version control.
##
## Get latest from https://github.com/FerroxLabs/ijfw

# IJFW runtime state — per-install, not source
.ijfw/

# Team layer — committed so conventions ride along with the repo
!.ijfw/team/

# User-project IJFW runtime artifacts (sessions, dump, metrics, etc.)
ijfw/

# IJFW runtime database and derived indexes
*.db
*.db-journal

# Raw result blobs and session receipts — NEVER commit
raw/
receipts/

# Optional: share wiki knowledge with the team
# !ijfw/wiki/
